### What moves from the Mac app into snapmark-kit

The spec says the web and the extension draw with "the same renderer as the Mac app" from `snapmark-kit/annotations` (design 11 and 14.2). Today that renderer is inside `snapmark-app/src/editor.ts`: 61 KB, Fabric 7.4, a classic script with no import or export. The extraction comes before ScreenshotCanvas, ComparePanes and DrawingToolbar can be built, and the Mac app must then load the kit through its esbuild bundle. `md-notes.ts` already shows the bundled pattern.

| Mac source | What moves | Target | Mac callers that change |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `editor.ts` item read and write (about lines 930 to 970), `shared.d.ts` `EditState` | The marks format, `{ t: 'arrow' \| 'marker' \| 'card' \| 'path' \| 'redact' \| 'cut', … }`. **Untyped today** (`items: unknown[]`). It becomes a versioned schema, because web, extension and Mac must read the same marks (sync, J7) | `packages/annotations/src/format.ts`, schema in `packages/contracts` | `editor.ts`, `main.ts` (stash and `state.json`), `sessions.ts` (`NNN.json` beside each entry). **Extract this first** |
| `tools.ts` | `GROUPS`, `ToolDef`, `ToolGroup`, `RED`, `YELLOW`, `capFor`, `keysFor`; it changes from a classic script with `module.exports` to ESM. One label per tool fixes "Hatched Area" against "Remove area" | `packages/annotations/src/tools.ts` | `bar.ts`, `editor.ts`, `keys.ts`, `main.ts`, `shortcuts.ts`, `editor.html`, `shortcuts.html`, `test/keys.test.ts`, `test/smoke.ts` |
| `editor.ts` shape classes | `Glyph` and `drawGlyph` (cross, hatch, highlight), `Arrow` and `arrowHead`, `Marker` and `drawMarker` (numbered references), `Card` and `bubbleTail`, `rect` | `packages/annotations/src/shapes/` | `editor.ts` |
| `editor.ts` tool behaviour | `redact` and `makeRedact` (pixelate), `cut`, `makeCut`, `edge` and `relink` (Cut & move with ghost and arrow), `drawGhost`, `cursorFor`, the undo and redo stacks | `packages/annotations/src/tools/`, `history.ts` | `editor.ts` |
| `editor.ts` colours | `PALETTE`, `CARD_BG`, the presets and custom colours (the panel UI becomes part of DrawingToolbar). The remove red and highlight yellow need tokens (Missing guidelines) | `packages/annotations/src/palette.ts` | `editor.ts` |
| `redact.ts` | `findSecrets`, `luhn`, `iban`, `secretBoxes` (pure, tested in Node) | `packages/redaction` (design 11) | `editor.ts`; `ocr.ts` stays in the Mac app because it is native OCR |
| `keys.ts` | The pattern, not the code: keys as data in one table read by the handlers and the shortcuts window. CommandMenu and ShortcutsDialog copy the idea with web keys | stays in the Mac app | none |
| `md-notes.ts` (Milkdown) | Could serve the Composer's Markdown subset. Not planned; decide in the plan | candidate for `packages/ui` | none in release 1 |
